fail[4]: Every level of this line has one node, so you see all of them: [1, 2, 3, 4].
fail[5]: The lesson's tree: 5, 8, 9, then 2 from the left subtree.
error[AttributeError]: Return [] for an empty tree, and only queue children that exist.
hint: Use rounds: read `size = len(queue)` and number the nodes with `for i in range(size)`.
hint: The rightmost node is the last one the round takes.
hint: Append `node.val` when `i == size - 1`.
right: A round takes its level from left to right, so the last node, `i == size - 1`, is the one you see from the right, wherever it hangs. O(n).
wrong: Following right links from the root misses nodes that stick out further down on the left. Run the level loop and keep the last node of every round.

